<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="4.799" dur="4.321">announcing [music] the arrival of His</text><text start="6.24" dur="4.479">Excellency Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr.,</text><text start="9.12" dur="4.559">President of the Republic of the [music]</text><text start="10.719" dur="4.96">Philippines, and Honorable Donald J.</text><text start="13.679" dur="4.641">Trump, President of [music] the United</text><text start="15.679" dur="7.321">States of America, together with First</text><text start="18.32" dur="4.68">Lady Louise Aronetta Marcos.</text><text start="25.119" dur="3">Heat. Heat.</text><text start="54.365" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="68.24" dur="4.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Ladies and [music] gentlemen, please be</text><text start="69.92" dur="3">seated.</text><text start="87.28" dur="7.36">May we invite his excellency Ferdinand</text><text start="90" dur="6.64">R. Marcos Jr. to deliver his remarks.</text><text start="94.64" dur="4.24">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr. President, distinguished guests,</text><text start="96.64" dur="4.799">ladies and gentlemen, it is a great</text><text start="98.88" dur="5.04">pleasure to welcome President Donald J.</text><text start="101.439" dur="5.121">Trump back to the Philippines to host a</text><text start="103.92" dur="4.239">state lunchon in his honor. Mr.</text><text start="106.56" dur="4.48">President, we are very pleased to have</text><text start="108.159" dur="5.201">you with us once again. Your visit comes</text><text start="111.04" dur="3.84">at a particularly meaningful time as the</text><text start="113.36" dur="3.759">Philippines and the United States</text><text start="114.88" dur="5.12">commemorate 80 years of diplomatic</text><text start="117.119" dur="6.161">relations and 75 years of our alliance</text><text start="120" dur="5.04">under the mutual defense treaty. These</text><text start="123.28" dur="3.76">anniversaries remind us that the</text><text start="125.04" dur="4.24">relationship between our two countries</text><text start="127.04" dur="5.12">is not only one of governments and</text><text start="129.28" dur="6.72">institutions. It is also a relationship</text><text start="132.16" dur="6.159">between peoples built over generations.</text><text start="136" dur="5.52">Strengthened by shared sacrifice,</text><text start="138.319" dur="6.56">enduring friendships, family ties, and a</text><text start="141.52" dur="5.6">deep sense of familiarity and trust,</text><text start="144.879" dur="4.08">Filipinos and Americans have stood side</text><text start="147.12" dur="3.92">by side through some of the most</text><text start="148.959" dur="5.201">consequential moments in our shared</text><text start="151.04" dur="5.839">history. That bond has endured because</text><text start="154.16" dur="4.799">it has continued to grow and adapt with</text><text start="156.879" dur="4.72">each generation.</text><text start="158.959" dur="5.441">Today, we celebrate that history, but we</text><text start="161.599" dur="5.201">also look ahead with optimism. Our</text><text start="164.4" dur="5.04">partnership today extends well beyond</text><text start="166.8" dur="5.76">defense and security. We are building</text><text start="169.44" dur="5.28">stronger ties in trade, investment, in</text><text start="172.56" dur="4.88">energy, in technology, resilient supply</text><text start="174.72" dur="4.64">chains, education, many other areas that</text><text start="177.44" dur="5.36">directly affect the lives and the</text><text start="179.36" dur="5.76">aspirations of both our peoples. Mr.</text><text start="182.8" dur="5.76">President, the Philippines deeply values</text><text start="185.12" dur="7.28">the United States as a trusted friend, a</text><text start="188.56" dur="6">steadfast partner, and an enduring ally.</text><text start="192.4" dur="3.839">We also value the personal engagement</text><text start="194.56" dur="3.92">and commitment that you have brought to</text><text start="196.239" dur="5.201">our relationship, ensuring that both our</text><text start="198.48" dur="4.88">peoples are safer, stronger, and more</text><text start="201.44" dur="4.32">prosperous.</text><text start="203.36" dur="4.48">I&amp;#39;m confident that your visit will give</text><text start="205.76" dur="4">fresh momentum to our partnership and</text><text start="207.84" dur="4.24">open new opportunities for our two</text><text start="209.76" dur="4.96">countries to work even more closely</text><text start="212.08" dur="5.12">together for our peoples, for our</text><text start="214.72" dur="6.4">region, for the peace and prosperity</text><text start="217.2" dur="6.56">that we all seek. Mr. President, on</text><text start="221.12" dur="5.119">behalf of the people of the Philippines,</text><text start="223.76" dur="4.96">I extend to you once again our warmest</text><text start="226.239" dur="5.201">welcome. We hope you feel very much at</text><text start="228.72" dur="4.96">home here in the Philippines. May I now</text><text start="231.44" dur="4.24">invite everyone to raise their glasses</text><text start="233.68" dur="4.4">to the good health and success of</text><text start="235.68" dur="5.119">President Trump, to the enduring</text><text start="238.08" dur="7.12">friendship between Filipino and American</text><text start="240.799" dur="6.881">peoples, to an even stronger and dynamic</text><text start="245.2" dur="4.399">Philippines United alliance in the years</text><text start="247.68" dur="4.919">ahead.</text><text start="249.599" dur="3">Filipinos.</text><text start="253.439" dur="3.72">Cheers, sir.</text><text start="266.24" dur="5.84">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; May we now invite the Honorable Donald</text><text start="268.56" dur="5.28">J. Trump to deliver his remarks.</text><text start="272.08" dur="5.04">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, thank you very much. It&amp;#39;s a great</text><text start="273.84" dur="5.6">honor to be here. President Marcus,</text><text start="277.12" dur="4.24">Madame First Lady, thank you for your</text><text start="279.44" dur="3.44">magnificent welcome back to this</text><text start="281.36" dur="3.36">exceptionally</text><text start="282.88" dur="5.039">beautiful country. It really is. It&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="284.72" dur="4.56">beautiful place and a lot of people are</text><text start="287.919" dur="3.121">watching what&amp;#39;s happening today and</text><text start="289.28" dur="4.72">they&amp;#39;ll be coming here. This is a place</text><text start="291.04" dur="4.879">of great opportunity and potential.</text><text start="294" dur="4.56">It&amp;#39;s a special honor to visit you here</text><text start="295.919" dur="5.041">within the walls of this storied palace</text><text start="298.56" dur="5.04">where some of the greatest Filipino and</text><text start="300.96" dur="4.32">American heroes before us have walked</text><text start="303.6" dur="3.68">and worked together to defend the</text><text start="305.28" dur="5.359">freedom and glory of both of our</text><text start="307.28" dur="6.56">countries. It&amp;#39;s got tremendous history</text><text start="310.639" dur="5.521">behind it. I got a tour by the president</text><text start="313.84" dur="3.919">and it was quite something. The bond</text><text start="316.16" dur="4.64">between the United States and the</text><text start="317.759" dur="6.481">Philippines is cherished and unique. And</text><text start="320.8" dur="6.08">the alliance that we have, and it&amp;#39;s born</text><text start="324.24" dur="4.72">out of a shared love of liberty was</text><text start="326.88" dur="5.52">proven across the generations, tempered</text><text start="328.96" dur="6">in the fine battle and sustained by a</text><text start="332.4" dur="5.44">mutual commitment to prosperity and</text><text start="334.96" dur="4.4">peace for all of our people. And we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="337.84" dur="3.359">worked together beautifully. And we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="339.36" dur="4.399">working together better now than ever</text><text start="341.199" dur="4.081">before. And we&amp;#39;ve just consummated a</text><text start="343.759" dur="5.121">very big trade deal, the biggest trade</text><text start="345.28" dur="5.359">deal we&amp;#39;ve ever made by far. And it&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="348.88" dur="5.44">fair deal for both countries. And we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="350.639" dur="4.881">very happy with it. And uh we didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="354.32" dur="3.599">know that that was going to take place,</text><text start="355.52" dur="5.44">but it took place very quickly. And it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="357.919" dur="5.12">a magnificent deal for both. So today,</text><text start="360.96" dur="4.799">under the leadership of President Marcus</text><text start="363.039" dur="4.801">and myself, I&amp;#39;m proud to say that we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="365.759" dur="4.16">making the alliance between the United</text><text start="367.84" dur="4.479">States and the Philippines much stronger</text><text start="369.919" dur="4.72">than it&amp;#39;s ever been before, especially</text><text start="372.319" dur="4.481">with the consummation of this deal.</text><text start="374.639" dur="4.161">Generations ago, America ended the</text><text start="376.8" dur="4.56">Spanish tyranny and domination of these</text><text start="378.8" dur="4.239">islands and quickly laid the foundations</text><text start="381.36" dur="4.64">for a modern and independent</text><text start="383.039" dur="4.801">Philippines. From William Howard Taft to</text><text start="386" dur="4.8">Dwight D. Eisenhower, some of the best</text><text start="387.84" dur="6.479">minds and foremost leaders of our nation</text><text start="390.8" dur="5.2">and that our nation has ever produced</text><text start="394.319" dur="4">have just poured their hearts and their</text><text start="396" dur="4.8">souls. They always knew that this was a</text><text start="398.319" dur="4.401">place of great potential. We&amp;#39;ve had a</text><text start="400.8" dur="3.119">lot of presidents look upon it, but I</text><text start="402.72" dur="3.759">don&amp;#39;t think there&amp;#39;s ever been a time</text><text start="403.919" dur="5.681">like this, frankly. And of course, it</text><text start="406.479" dur="5.761">was right here, this very palace that</text><text start="409.6" dur="6.159">President Quaison bestowed General</text><text start="412.24" dur="5.76">Douglas MacArthur with a gold baton and</text><text start="415.759" dur="4">the rank of field marshal in the</text><text start="418" dur="4.319">Philippine Army. I&amp;#39;d like to have you do</text><text start="419.759" dur="4.241">that to me if you don&amp;#39;t mind. I love</text><text start="422.319" dur="4.961">that. I mean, why the hell shouldn&amp;#39;t I</text><text start="424" dur="6.72">get that? But to help prepare the proud</text><text start="427.28" dur="5.759">nation to defend the land and really the</text><text start="430.72" dur="4.4">land of their fathers. And when the</text><text start="433.039" dur="7.041">battle came from the streets of Manila</text><text start="435.12" dur="8.32">to the steep cliffs of Corridor to the</text><text start="440.08" dur="5.76">immortal heroes of Baton, brave American</text><text start="443.44" dur="5.12">and Filipino sons shed their blood into</text><text start="445.84" dur="5.84">the same sand, rock and mud to defend</text><text start="448.56" dur="6.32">this land and the land of our brothers</text><text start="451.68" dur="4.799">and our sisters and our mothers, our</text><text start="454.88" dur="5.439">fathers.</text><text start="456.479" dur="6.081">260,000 Philippine heroes fought beneath</text><text start="460.319" dur="4.32">the stars and stripes of World War II</text><text start="462.56" dur="4.8">and countless American service members</text><text start="464.639" dur="6.321">gave their lives to fulfill that famous</text><text start="467.36" dur="6.72">pledge of MacArthur. I shall return. He</text><text start="470.96" dur="5.04">said, I shall return. because of the</text><text start="474.08" dur="5.44">sacrifice of those who gave everything</text><text start="476" dur="6.08">to keep that vow. Today, the Philippines</text><text start="479.52" dur="5.04">are free and Manila is home to the</text><text start="482.08" dur="4.399">largest overseas American military</text><text start="484.56" dur="4.479">cemetery anywhere in the world. Many</text><text start="486.479" dur="4.241">people died defending the Philippines</text><text start="489.039" dur="4.56">and that&amp;#39;s why I&amp;#39;m so happy that we were</text><text start="490.72" dur="5.52">able to do a deal today. This is the</text><text start="493.599" dur="6.16">kind of history that binds nations</text><text start="496.24" dur="6.32">forever. And today we really uh we look</text><text start="499.759" dur="5.681">to those before us. President Marcos and</text><text start="502.56" dur="5.68">I continue to work to defend the peace</text><text start="505.44" dur="6.479">our ancestors won and they so bravely</text><text start="508.24" dur="9.12">won. The the level of hardship, the lab</text><text start="511.919" dur="8.081">level of terror and the level of love in</text><text start="517.36" dur="4.88">this country has been extraordinary. And</text><text start="520" dur="3.839">the freedom our children will inherit</text><text start="522.24" dur="4.24">for generations to come. and they&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="523.839" dur="4.481">look to the Philippines as just a very</text><text start="526.48" dur="5.12">important place even in American</text><text start="528.32" dur="6.48">history. And now it becomes with today&amp;#39;s</text><text start="531.6" dur="6.239">deal, it becomes more important and more</text><text start="534.8" dur="5.36">united. Our two nations along with Japan</text><text start="537.839" dur="5.12">recently launched the Luzon Economic</text><text start="540.16" dur="5.6">Guard to facilitate critically needed</text><text start="542.959" dur="5.121">infrastructure in the central crossroads</text><text start="545.76" dur="4.72">of the world. And this year we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="548.08" dur="5.439">celebrating the 75th anniversary of our</text><text start="550.48" dur="5.12">mutual defense agreement which we marked</text><text start="553.519" dur="4.241">by conducting our largest ever joint</text><text start="555.6" dur="5.84">exercise bringing together all of our</text><text start="557.76" dur="5.36">forces across air, land, sea, cyber, and</text><text start="561.44" dur="4.079">space.</text><text start="563.12" dur="5.52">Although we are separated by thousands</text><text start="565.519" dur="5.601">of miles, and when I say thousands, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="568.64" dur="5.12">thousands and thousands of miles far</text><text start="571.12" dur="4.48">away, but it really seems close to me</text><text start="573.76" dur="3.68">because of the relationship. It doesn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="575.6" dur="5.2">seem far away, but our countries are</text><text start="577.44" dur="6.24">still united by common interests and by</text><text start="580.8" dur="4.96">the even more enduring ties of culture</text><text start="583.68" dur="5.279">and commerce and the values that first</text><text start="585.76" dur="5.84">brought us together so long ago. And as</text><text start="588.959" dur="4.801">we can see in the beautiful Christmas</text><text start="591.6" dur="4.48">decorations and Christmas is such a big</text><text start="593.76" dur="5.04">part of the Philippines. I came and I</text><text start="596.08" dur="4.319">said, &amp;quot;Wow, that&amp;#39;s really something.&amp;quot;</text><text start="598.8" dur="3.039">They didn&amp;#39;t talk about taking Christmas</text><text start="600.399" dur="4">away. You know, in our country, they</text><text start="601.839" dur="6.481">said, &amp;quot;Let&amp;#39;s not use Christmas anymore.&amp;quot;</text><text start="604.399" dur="5.921">In 2016, we ended that. That was ended.</text><text start="608.32" dur="3.68">But they treat they treat Christmas with</text><text start="610.32" dur="3.6">great love and respect in the</text><text start="612" dur="4.88">Philippines. Decorations displayed</text><text start="613.92" dur="7.84">throughout this palace and all of Manila</text><text start="616.88" dur="9.12">show that our people are also united by</text><text start="621.76" dur="6.8">faith in God and uh the Filipinos are</text><text start="626" dur="4.88">with us all the way. Religion, religion</text><text start="628.56" dur="4.64">is a very big part of the Philippines.</text><text start="630.88" dur="5.12">So, President Marcos and Madame First</text><text start="633.2" dur="4.879">Lady, two incredible people. Thank you</text><text start="636" dur="4.64">again for your extraordinary welcome and</text><text start="638.079" dur="5.921">continued friendship. And I ask everyone</text><text start="640.64" dur="7.12">to please join me in raising a toast.</text><text start="644" dur="5.839">May our alliance stand as strong as the</text><text start="647.76" dur="4">heroes who forged it. And together, may</text><text start="649.839" dur="4.56">we lead the United States and the</text><text start="651.76" dur="5.04">Philippines toward a future of even</text><text start="654.399" dur="4.321">greater safety, prosperity, and peace.</text><text start="656.8" dur="3.599">These are wonderful people. This is a</text><text start="658.72" dur="3.2">wonderful place and it&amp;#39;s an honor to be</text><text start="660.399" dur="2.161">here. Thank you very much.</text><text start="661.92" dur="1.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you very much.</text><text start="662.56" dur="4.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you very much.</text><text start="663.68" dur="3.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you. Cheers, sir.</text><text start="668.399" dur="4.281">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you. Thank you very much.</text><text start="679.839" dur="4.081">Thank you, your excellencies,</text><text start="682.24" dur="3.44">distinguished guests, ladies and</text><text start="683.92" dur="4.76">gentlemen, we shall now begin the</text><text start="685.68" dur="3">lunchon.</text></transcript>